# probes/Dockerfile installs the published payload and never COPYs from this
# context. This file only keeps local credentials and build artifacts out of the
# build context (Docker ignores .gitignore), e.g. before sending it to a remote
# daemon. It stays narrow on purpose: Dockerfile.probe-test is documented to
# build from this directory too and needs the agent sources.
.env
**/.env
**/probe.env
agent/dist/
